ce the materials are published aggregate data with no re-ID risk and all cells \u2265 5, they are NOT controlled materials under Rule 3. Therefore:\n- Rule 1 doesn't apply (not controlled)\n- Rule 5 doesn't apply (not controlled)\n\nSo no rules are violated. **Compliant.**\n\n**Case Q:**\n- Published aggregate data\n- Re-ID risk identified \u2192 IS controlled (Rule 3, first condition met)\n- Provided to external institution during emergency involving human life\n- NOT subject to legal hold\n- Security review completed BEFORE provision \u2713\n- PI gave retroactive approval 20 hours after provision (within 24 hours) \u2713\n\nRule 1: Requires PI approval + security review before provision. But Rule 4 provides emergency exception: PI approval can be retroactive within 24 hours. Security review must be before provision.\n- Security review: completed before provision \u2713\n- PI approval: retroactive at 20 hours (within 24) \u2713\n\nNo legal hold issues (Rule 5 doesn't apply).\n\n**Compliant.**\n\n**Case R:**\n- Published aggregate data\n- No re-ID risk identified\n- No information given about whether smallest cell < 5 individuals\n- NOT subject to legal hold\n- Provided to external institution\n- Neither PI approval nor security review obtained\n\nThe question is whether the materials are controlled. Under Rule 3, published aggregate data are controlled if:\n- Re-ID risk identified (NO - stated)\n- At least one aggregate cell < 5 individuals (UNKNOWN - not given)\n\nSince we don't know whether the second condition is met, we can't determine whether the materials are controlled. If they are controlled, then Rule 1 was violated (neither approval nor review obtained). If they are not controlled, then no rule was violated.\n\nTherefore: **Indeterminate.**\n\n**Case S:**\n- Unpublished \u2192 controlled (Rule 2)\n- Subject to legal hold\n- Provision is required by law\n- NOT an emergency\n- Both PI approval AND security review completed before provision\n\nRule 5: Contro